-- title:
--   Smooth supersingular point stalk from an affine chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa(A),M')$ over $\kappa(A)=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa(A)$, assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' =: F$, and fix an element $s$ of $W$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ such that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0\cap A$, and assume $\kappa(A)$ algebraically closed. Let $K_b$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$, and $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by a non-zero $\varpi_b$. Then, $F$ being viewed as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0=F$ (the join of $k_0$-adjoin of the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $F_0$ is everything) and such that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ any $K'$-linearly independent family $c_1,\dots,c_m\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ admits no non-trivial relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ with $a_i$ in the join of $k_0$-adjoin of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$; for every subring $B$ of $F$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion $A_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to F$, with $B$ contained in the join of $k_0$-adjoin of the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$ and with that join equal to the fraction field of $B$, $B$ formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, $\dim B/\varpi_b B\le 1$, $B$ contained in $W_0$, $\varpi_b$ prime in $B$, and $W_0$ the set of $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; and for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa(A)$, every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ in $F$ with residue target $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $\mathcal O_R$ of $F$ with surjective residue map to $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ and $\kappa(A)$) with $\mathcal O_R\cap F_0=W_0$ and $B\subseteq\mathcal O_R$ such that every element of $F_{ss}$ is a ratio of residues of elements of $B$, and every place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa(A)$ whose valuation subring contains all residues of $B$: there exist a subring $S$ of $F$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi:A_b[X]\to S$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi:S\to\kappa(A)$ such that $S$ contains the image of $A_b$, $\varphi(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for $a\in A_b$, $\chi(\varphi(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$, $\chi(\varphi(X))=0$; $S$ is local with $\ker\chi$ its maximal ideal; $S$ lies in the join of $k_0$-adjoin of the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$, and that join is the fraction field of $S$; $\varphi$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S\subseteq\mathcal O_R$ with $\mathfrak m_R\cap S$ the set of multiples of $\varphi(C\,\varpi_b)$; for every $f\in S$ the residue $R$-reduction of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi(f)$ under $\kappa(A)\to\kappa(Q)$; $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the reduction of $\varphi(X)$ equals $1$; and finally $B\subseteq S$, with $S$ consisting exactly of the quotients $g/h$, $g,h\in B$, whose denominator has non-zero residue at $Q$.
--
--   This produces, at a smooth point of the supersingular fibre singled out by a place $Q$, the local ring $S$ of the model read off the affine chart $B$, together with an étale coordinate $\varphi:A_b[X]\to S$ whose variable reduces to a uniformiser at $Q$ and a residue character $\chi:S\to\kappa(A)$ compatible with the regular prolongation $R$. It is the $q=2$ case, with the prime assumption $q=2$ in place of $5\le q$, and it feeds the construction of the base smooth point stalks at full level and their localisations.
